Z||000012||fierosound||01-16-2000||05:22 PM||||The sportier the car - the more dangerous to paint it "ARREST ME RED".  Police seem to watch more closely...<P>I've had cars of many different colors.  Police don't look twice at white, grey, or blue cars.  I settled on a burgundy/grey 87 GT because I liked that combination the best.  I haven't had police "watching me"..<P>Just a thought.  Anyone else notice car color making a difference in police attitudes?||||reg||10
Z||000013||Cooter||01-16-2000||05:59 PM||||It is funny that you would ask. My brother is a policeman and when his car was broke down, he drove my Fiero for "a few days"- that turned out to be several weeks! He got pulled over at least 5 times. Of course, he drives like a demon. Since I got my car back, I have not had a policeman give it a second look.||||reg||1
Z||000014||lowCG||01-16-2000||11:08 PM||||A neat way to get a canary yellow is to start with a safety yellow(Corvette yellow,or something strong) base coat,then put a clear with platinum pearl over it.The platinum pearl shades the color up to a pale or canary color.I did this on one of my bike frames back in '87 and wanted to try it on a car sometime.||||reg||1
